BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (Acceptable orientations:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 707 Td (- Horizontal pipe, with the electronics housing on the side \(3 o'clock or 9 o'clock) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 694 Td (   position\) so that the optical windows are not at the top or bottom of the pipe. This is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 681 Td (   the preferred orientation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (- Vertical pipe with upward flow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 655 Td (Do not install on vertical pipe with downward flow unless there is enough back pressure to keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 642 Td (the pipe full at all times. Do not install with the electronics housing directly underneath the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 629 Td (pipe, where leaks from the flanges can drip onto the cable glands.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 607 Td (Lift the meter into position with the flange covers still fitted, remove the covers, insert the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 594 Td (gaskets and fit the bolts finger tight. Tighten the bolts as described in section 11.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 571 Td (7.1 Gaskets) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 549 Td (Use gaskets with an inside diameter no smaller than the pipe bore. A gasket that protrudes into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 536 Td (the bore creates turbulence directly upstream of the optical windows and causes L-204 low) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 523 Td (signal quality warnings. For hot water applications above 80 \260C, use graphite-faced) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 510 Td (spiral-wound or reinforced graphite gaskets. Compressed fibre gaskets are acceptable up to 80) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 497 Td (\260C.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 472 Td (8. Electrical installation) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 449 Td (8.1 Cable and glands) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 427 Td (Use screened twisted-pair instrument cable with a conductor cross-section of 0.5 to 1.5 mm\262.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 414 Td (For the RS-485 bus, use cable with a characteristic impedance of 120 ohm. Terminate the screen) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 401 Td (at the meter end in the cable gland \(360-degree termination\) and at the control system end only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388 Td (if the site earthing philosophy requires it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 366 Td (Unused cable entries must be closed with the supplied M20 blanking plug to maintain IP67.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 343 Td (8.2 Terminal assignment) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 322 Td (Terminal | Function | Notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 310 Td (1 | +24 VDC supply | 24 VDC \26110%, 5.5 W) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 298 Td (2 | 0 V supply |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 286 Td (3 | 4-20 mA / HART + | Active or passive, selected in menu) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 274 Td (4 | 4-20 mA / HART - |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 262 Td (5 | Pulse output + | Open collector, max 30 VDC, 100 mA, max 2 kHz) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 250 Td (6 | Pulse output - |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 238 Td (7 | RS-485 A \(D+\) | Modbus RTU) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 226 Td (8 | RS-485 B \(D-\) | Modbus RTU) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 214 Td (9 | Functional earth / screen |) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 192 Td (The RS-485 termination resistor \(120 ohm\) is switched on with DIP switch S1 on the terminal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 179 Td (board. Enable it only on the last device of the bus.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 156 Td (8.3 Power) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 134 Td (The LF-60P draws 5.5 W at 24 VDC, around 230 mA, plus an inrush of up to 900 mA for 20 ms. Size) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 121 Td (the supply and fuse accordingly. The meter starts measuring about 25 seconds after power is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 108 Td (applied; the display shows the firmware version \(1.9.0\) during start-up.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 83 Td (9. Grounding and bonding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 61 Td (Correct grounding is the single most important factor for stable optical signal processing on) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
