12 0 obj
<< /Length 3874 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (1. Enter the service passcode \(see section 13\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (2. Go to Menu > Setup > Outputs > HART > Poll Address and set the polling address. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (   default is 0, which keeps the loop current active. Addresses 1 to 63 put the output into) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (   multidrop mode with a fixed 4 mA current.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (3. Go to Menu > Setup > Outputs > HART > Tag and enter the long tag \(up to 32 characters\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (   The short tag is limited to 8 characters and is set from the host system.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 651 Td (4. Go to Menu > Setup > Outputs > HART > Variable Map to assign the dynamic variables. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 638 Td (   factory mapping is PV volume flow, SV forward totaliser, TV process pressure, QV fluid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 625 Td (   temperature.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612 Td (5. If burst mode is required, enable it under Menu > Setup > Outputs > HART > Burst. Burst) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 599 Td (   mode is disabled by default.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 585 Td (10.3 Loop test) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 563 Td (Use Menu > Diagnostics > Loop Test to force the output to 4, 12 and 20 mA and confirm the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 550 Td (reading at the control system. The loop test times out after 10 minutes and returns the output) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 537 Td (to normal operation.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 512 Td (11. Flange bolting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 490 Td (Flange joints on the LF-60P must be tightened in a controlled sequence to the values below.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 477 Td (Under-tightening causes leaks at operating pressure. Over-tightening distorts the measuring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 464 Td (tube flanges and can crack the window seats, which is not covered by warranty.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 441 Td (11.1 Torque values) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 419 Td (The values apply to EN 1092-1 PN40 flanges, lightly oiled carbon steel or stainless steel bolts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 406 Td (\(property class 8.8 or A4-80\), and graphite-faced or compressed fibre gaskets. For PTFE) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 393 Td (gaskets, reduce the values by 20%.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 372 Td (Meter size | Bolts | Torque) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 360 Td (DN25 | 4 x M12 | 45 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 348 Td (DN40 | 4 x M16 | 75 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 336 Td (DN50 | 4 x M16 | 85 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 324 Td (DN65 | 8 x M16 | 80 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 312 Td (DN80 | 8 x M16 | 95 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 300 Td (DN100 | 8 x M20 | 140 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 288 Td (DN125 | 8 x M24 | 210 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 276 Td (DN150 | 8 x M24 | 250 N m) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 254 Td (For meters with ASME Class 300 flanges, use the torque values in the ASME supplement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 241 Td (LF-ASME-300, which is supplied with the meter.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 218 Td (11.2 Tightening sequence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 196 Td (1. Fit all bolts finger tight and check that the gaskets are centred.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 183 Td (2. Tighten in a cross \(star\) pattern to 30% of the final torque.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 170 Td (3. Repeat the cross pattern to 60% of the final torque.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 157 Td (4. Repeat the cross pattern to 100% of the final torque.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 144 Td (5. Make one final circular pass at 100% to check that no bolt turns further.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 131 Td (6. Pressure test the line to 1.5 times the design pressure, but never above 60 bar.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 118 Td (7. For lines operating above 80 \260C, re-check the torque after the first heat-up and cool-down) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 105 Td (   cycle.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 92 Td (Use a calibrated torque wrench. Do not use impact tools.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 67 Td (12. Zero-point adjustment) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
13 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 3 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 612 792] /Contents 12 0 R /Resources << /Font << /F1 1 0 R /F2 2 0 R >> >> >>
endobj
14 0 obj
<< /Length 4751 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (The LF-60P is factory calibrated on a water flow rig traceable to national standards, and a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (zero-point adjustment is not normally required. Carry out a zero-point adjustment after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (installation only if the meter shows a flow reading above 0.5 cm/s when the line is known to be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (full and completely stationary.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (1. Make sure the measuring tube is completely full and that there is no flow. Close valves) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 655 Td (   both upstream and downstream of the meter; a closed downstream valve alone is not enough.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 642 Td (2. Wait at least 5 minutes for the fluid to settle and, for hot lines, for the temperature to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 629 Td (   stabilise.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 616 Td (3. Enter the service passcode.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 603 Td (4. Go to Menu > Service > Calibration > Zero Adjust and confirm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 590 Td (5. The meter averages the signal for 60 seconds and stores the new zero offset. The display) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 577 Td (   shows the offset in cm/s.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 564 Td (6. If the offset is larger than \2612.0 cm/s, the adjustment is rejected. Check for leaking) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 551 Td (   valves, air in the line and grounding \(section 9\) before trying again.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 538 Td (The previous zero offset can be restored under Menu > Service > Calibration > Restore Factory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 525 Td (Zero.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 502 Td (12.1 In-situ verification and window inspection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 480 Td (The LF-60P runs a continuous self-check of the LED emitter current, receiver gain and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 467 Td (correlation quality. The results can be read under Menu > Diagnostics > Verification, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 454 Td (produces a pass or fail report with a four-digit verification code. Record the code at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 441 Td (commissioning; comparing later codes against the commissioning value shows whether the optical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 428 Td (path has degraded. Asset management systems can read the same report over HART \(device-specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 415 Td (command 140\) or Modbus.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 393 Td (Window fouling shows as a gradual fall in signal quality. Under normal conditions the signal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 380 Td (quality indicator reads between 85% and 100%. Below 60%, the meter raises L-204; below 40% the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 367 Td (flow reading is held at its last good value and the output goes to the configured fail-safe) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 354 Td (current \(3.6 mA by default, adjustable to 21.0 mA under Menu > Setup > Outputs > Current >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 341 Td (Fail-safe\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 319 Td (On fluids that contain oils, biofilm or scale-forming minerals, plan an inspection of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 306 Td (sapphire windows every 12 months. The windows can be inspected with a borescope through a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 293 Td (flange after isolating and draining the line, without removing the meter. Clean with isopropyl) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 280 Td (alcohol; for mineral scale, use a 5% citric acid solution followed by a clean water rinse. Do) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 267 Td (not use abrasive pads, wire brushes or hydrochloric acid, which will damage the window seals.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 244 Td (12.2 Low-flow cut-off and damping) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222 Td (The low-flow cut-off suppresses readings close to zero. The default is 0.02 m/s and can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 209 Td (changed under Menu > Setup > Measurement > Low Flow Cutoff. The damping time constant defaults) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 196 Td (to 2.0 seconds on the LF-60P and can be set between 0.2 and 60 seconds under Menu > Setup >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 183 Td (Measurement > Damping. Increase damping where the flow reading must be steady for control, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 170 Td (decrease it for fast batching.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 145 Td (13. Local display and security) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123 Td (The two-line display shows the flow rate on the first line and, by default, the forward) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 110 Td (totaliser on the second line. Press the right-hand key to scroll through velocity, reverse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 97 Td (totaliser, process pressure, fluid temperature and signal quality.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 75 Td (Configuration menus are protected by a four-digit service passcode. The factory default) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 62 Td (passcode for the LF-60P is 4060. Change it at commissioning under Menu > Service > Security >) Tj ET
endstream
